<!--
  ic_splash_icon.xml — Placeholder vector for the splash screen centre icon.

  IMPORTANT: Replace this with your actual app icon.
  The easiest way:
    1. In Android Studio → right-click res/ → New → Image Asset
    2. Choose "Launcher Icons (Adaptive and Legacy)"
    3. Import your icon-512.png as the source
    4. Android Studio generates all required mipmap densities + adaptive icon

  Alternatively, copy public/icons/icon-512.png to:
    app/src/main/res/drawable/ic_splash_icon.png
  and update themes.xml to reference @drawable/ic_splash_icon

  This placeholder draws the ForgeOS "F" lettermark in indigo.
-->
